# Niida et al. (2020, ApJ 904, 89), Table 3, "HSC S16A-Wide2" block; checked against arXiv:2010.00481v1
# Sample: photometric z ~ 5 quasar candidates in 81.8 deg^2 of HSC-SSP S16A Wide (19.1 < i < 24.1); N_corr = number after subtracting
#         the estimated Galactic-star contamination. Most objects have no spectroscopic redshift.
# Redshift: z ~ 5; M1450 computed assuming z = 4.9 (peak of the HSC completeness). File labelled z ~ 5 as in the paper.
# Magnitude definition: M1450; bins of Delta m_i = 0.5 mag
# Phi convention: linear Phi in units of 1e-8 cMpc^-3 mag^-1 (H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7), asymmetric errors (upper, lower)
# Note: Errors are Poisson; Gehrels (1986) intervals for bins with N_corr < 50 (the -22.57 bin has symmetric errors in the paper).
# Note: The two faintest bins (M1450 = -22.57 and -23.07, i > 23.1) may be contaminated by point-like galaxies and were excluded
#       from the paper's QLF fit (which uses M1450 < -23.32 only).
# Note: The SDSS DR7 bright-end points of the same table (the paper's own measurement from the SDSS DR7 quasar catalogue,
#       z = 4.5-5.2, 0.25-mag bins) are in the separate entry Niida2020_SDSS.
#
# M1450  Phi  UpperDelta  LowerDelta
